       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/rx933wn3761.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "the same stamp struck twice on this crop, once heavily and once so lightly that only the tops of the figures took ink. In the heavy impression the five figures read 1, 2, 1, 2 and a last figure with a closed counter above and below, so 8; the light impression left only the upper curl of that figure, which alone would read 6 and would give 1926. Both impressions carry the same short double-dash mark before the first figure, so that mark belongs to the stamp device rather than being a figure. Read as 12.1.28 with the separators dropped."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
